{"authored" [{"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/a50acd7e54d52f6284962cb81a5f662321b045a5d533470186719ad2a91ab18b.png)\n\nGiven the sets $Y={△,◻,♣,♡}$ and  $Z={△,◻,♡,♢,♠}$ shown above, find $Z∖Y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $Z∖Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $Z$ but not $Y.$ To represent $Z∖Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Z$ but not $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/45a15beb8833e2974706a04b0cdfd81dcdda4b92323f0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39" "basis"