veloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{♠,♢}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{♣}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{♠,♢}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{12,24…}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{4,8,16,20,…}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2ffba6d9726b7a66223df3064e63623615cad89c302af47c165e2857a10811" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7167.json" "file_sha256" "64e9cdcf35df4720b46d83afcbaa69f08f57800671f8132fb236db6e623639c6" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7167.json" "file_sha256" "64e9cdcf35df4720b46d83afcbaa69f08f57800671f8132fb236db6e623639c6" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the sets $X = \\{ 2, 5, 7, 8 \\},$ $Y = \\{ 1, 3, 5 \\},$ and $Z = \\{ 2, 4, 6, 8 \\},$ find $X \\setminus Y,$ $Y \\setminus Z,$ and $Z \\setminus X.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7159.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cc88a7a8e1c95d3f28d03c43eff3dc570489e6f0a2c26b2b83db0d90dbc1" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X,$ so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={2,5,7,8}-{1,3,5} \\\\  & ={2,7,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z.$ Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∖Z & =Y-Z \\\\  & ={1,3,5}-{2,4,6,8} \\\\  & ={1,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z∖X & =Z-X \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}-{2,5,7,8} \\\\  & ={4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7159.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cc88a7a8e1c95d3f28d03c43eff3dc570489e6f0a2c26b2b83db0d90dbc1" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0.$ What is $A \\setminus B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7160.json" "file_sha256" "64d579f5640dd079be1f4d1c8a1cbdfbde9085a62adda1740262a34ab9ea0c9b" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\setminus B$ is the *difference* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $A$ but *not* in $B.$\n\nThe elements of $A$ that are also in $B$ are $12, 24, 36$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $A.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}-{6,12,18,24,30,36,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,28,32,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/example-7160.json" "file_sha256" "64d579f5640dd079be1f4d1c8a1cbdfbde9085a62adda1740262a34ab9ea0c9b" "basis" 1263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/a50acd7e54d52f6284962cb81a5f662321b045a5d533470186719ad2a91ab18b.png)\n\nGiven the sets $Y={△,◻,♣,♡}$ and  $Z={△,◻,♡,♢,♠}$ shown above, find $Z∖Y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $Z∖Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $Z$ but not $Y.$ To represent $Z∖Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Z$ but not $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/45a15beb8833e2974706a04b0cdfd81dcdda4b92323f0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{△,◻,♠}"] ["math" "{♠,◻,♣,♡}"] ["math" "{♠,♢,♣}"] ["math" "{♠,♢}"] ["math" "{♣}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{♠,♢}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/3b539190899ca580528fdbf7b5d3ef9925ade29f97f4b2f96b0f1394743f40a8.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={p,a,s,w,o,r,d}$ and $T={p,o,r,t,e,l},$ find $T∖S.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $T∖S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T∖S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT∖S={t,e,l}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b8