sy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-81754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{a,s,r}"] ["math" "{c,e,k}"] ["math" "{t,m,x,y,z}"] ["math" "{t,m}"] ["math" "{x,y,z}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{c,e,k}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $C={1,2,3,4,8,12,24}$ and $D={0,4,8,12,16,20,24},$ then $D∖C=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $D∖C$ is the set of all elements belonging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $4,8,12,24\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∖C & =D-C \\\\  & ={0,4,8,12,16,20,24}-{1,2,3,4,8,12,24} \\\\  & ={0,16,20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,1,2,3,16,20}"] ["math" "{0,1,2,3,4,8,12,16,20,24}"] ["math" "{0,16,20}"] ["math" "{1,2,3}"] ["math" "{4,8,12,24}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0,16,20}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $C={-3,-1,0,5,10}$ and $D={-2,-1,0,1}$, then $C∖D=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $C∖D$ is the set of all elements belonging to $C$ but *not* $D.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in D$ are also in $C,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={-3,-1,0,5,10}-{-2,-1,0,1} \\\\  & ={-3,5,10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-2,1}"] ["math" "{-3,1}"] ["math" "{-3,5,10}"] ["math" "{-3,5}"] ["math" "{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{-3,5,10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={3,6,9,12,15}$ an