successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $X={1,3,5,7}$ and $Y={1,2,3,4},$ then $Y-X=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $Y-X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y-X & ={1,2,3,4}-{1,3,5,7} \\\\  & ={2,4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{1,2}"] ["math" "{1,3}"] ["math" "{2,4}"] ["math" "{5,7}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{2,4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $C={-3,-1,0,5,10}$ and $D={-2,-1,0,1},$ then $D∖C=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $D∖C$ is the set of all elements belonging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∖C & =D-C \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0,1}-{-3,-1,0,5,10} \\\\  & ={-2,1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-2,1}"] ["math" "{-3,1}"] ["math" "{-3,5,10}"] ["math" "{-3,5}"] ["math" "{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-1227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{-2,1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $S$  be the set of all multiples of $2$ greater than $0$ and let $T$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $T∖S?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $2$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nS={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nT={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $T∖S$ is the *difference* of $T$ and $S,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $T$ but *not* in $S.$\n\nThe elements of $T$ that are also in $S$ are $4,8,12,16,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $4$). So, we must remove these elements from $T.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T∖S & ={4,8,12,16,…}-{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,2,6,10,14,…}"] ["math" "{0,4,8,12,16,…}"] ["math" "{2,4,10,14,…}"] ["math" "{4,8,12,16,…}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-105230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…}"] ["math" "{12,24…}"] ["math" "{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…}"] ["math" "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}"] ["math" "{4,8,16,20,…}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-81766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{4,8,16,20,…}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $E$  be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $2$ and let $F$  be  the set of all non-negative integer powers of $4.$  What is $F-E?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nE={1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, the powers of $4$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nF={1,4,16,64,256,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $F-E$ is the *difference* of $F$ and $E,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $F$ but *not* in $E.$\n\nAll elements of $F$ are also in $E.$  So, we must remove these elements from $F.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F-E & ={1,4,16,64,256,…}-{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{1,2,4,8,16,32,…}"] ["math" "{1,4,16,64,256,…}"] ["math" "{1}"] ["math" "{4,16,64,256,…}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-86705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $C$  be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $D$  be the the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $C∖D?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-80876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}-{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_A