40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-36195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={10,20,30,40,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B∖A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & ={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}-{10,20,30,40,…} \\\\  & ={5,15,25,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-36195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "498eaed7cb74b8e9ca1906ff6f0b7009bc228b2efce098ab69244f146946e86f"} {"question" "q-36195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-36195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,5,15,25,35,…}"] ["math" "{5,10,12,15,20,22,25,30,…}"] ["math" "{5,15,25,35,…}"] ["math" "{7,9,11,13,15,17,19,…}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "q-36195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{5,15,25,35,…}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/state.json" "file_sha256" "34f12ebe47c4212a9cbbfc8def424aa98671d40a6f8b859f4cac7377828bb33e"} {"question" "e-7167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7167.json" "file_sha256" "d70ed31d7c4396df80f966aeeeb8ddecf02ab0c4fba088fde9f0ebaa75303f48"} {"question" "e-7167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7167.json" "file_sha256" "d70ed31d7c4396df80f966aeeeb8ddecf02ab0c4fba088fde9f0ebaa75303f48"} {"question" "e-7159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the sets $X = \\{ 2, 5, 7, 8 \\},$ $Y = \\{ 1, 3, 5 \\},$ and $Z = \\{ 2, 4, 6, 8 \\},$ find $X \\setminus Y,$ $Y \\setminus Z,$ and $Z \\setminus X.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7159.json" "file_sha256" "57277833ddcb07b45b865cac6eb95ba71ebada9094ca2528223c55b4aed30015"} {"question" "e-7159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X,$ so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={2,5,7,8}-{1,3,5} \\\\  & ={2,7,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z.$ Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∖Z & =Y-Z \\\\  & ={1,3,5}-{2,4,6,8} \\\\  & ={1,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z∖X & =Z-X \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}-{2,5,7,8} \\\\  & ={4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7159.json" "file_sha256" "57277833ddcb07b45b865cac6eb95ba71ebada9094ca2528223c55b4aed30015"} {"question" "e-7160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0.$ What is $A \\setminus B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7160.json" "file_sha256" "ff2d60411a47501aa83b3f5017f01cdf98b5d68fecaa50ee64e84d1515125692"} {"question" "e-7160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\setminus B$ is the *difference* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $A$ but *not* in $B.$\n\nThe elements of $A$ that are also in $B$ are $12, 24, 36$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $A.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}-{6,12,18,24,30,36,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,28,32,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/example-7160.json" "file_sha256" "ff2d60411a47501aa83b3f5017f01cdf98b5d68fecaa50ee64e84d1515125692"}] "usage" {"q-36195" [] "e-7167" [] "q-81766" [] "q-105200" [] "e-7160" [] "e-7159" []} "basis" 2593 "retractions" [[17592186296422 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/a50acd7e54d52f6284962cb81a5f662321b045a5d533470186719ad2a91ab18b.png)\n\nGiven the sets $Y={△,◻,♣,♡}$ and  $Z={△,◻,♡,♢,♠}$ shown above, find $Z∖Y.$"] [17592186296422 :question/worked-solution "The difference $Z∖Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $Z$ but not $Y.$ To represent $Z∖Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Z$ but not $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/45a15beb8833e2974706a04b0cdfd81dcdda4b92323f0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$"] [17592186157706 :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0$. What is $B∖A$?"] [17592186157026 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$"] [17592186157026 :question/worked-solution "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186155489 17592186155490 17592186155491 17592186155492 17592186155493 17592186296424 17592186296425 17592186296426 17592186296427 17592186296428 17592186296501 17592186296502 17592186296503 17592186296504 17592186296505] "immutable_fields" [[17592186155488 :answer-field/correct] [17592186155488 :answer-field/id] [17592186155488 :answer-field/key] [17592186155488 :answer-field/type] [17592186296423 :answer-field/correct] [17592186296423 :answer-field/id] [17592186296423 :answer-field/key] [17592186296423 :answer-field/type] [17592186296500 :answer-field/correct] [17592186296500 :answer-field/id] [17592186296500 :answer-field/key] [17592186296500 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
